# Auto-deploy — local / git / EC2 stay in sync

After shipping code changes for GetStockReport, **do not leave production behind**.

## Default workflow

1. Finish the code change locally.
2. Commit when the user asks (or when they explicitly request deploy/ship/push-all).
3. **Push to `origin/main`.**
4. **Automatically deploy to the EC2 instance** so live matches git — do not wait to be asked.

Treat “done” as: local working tree (for that work) == `origin/main` == EC2 `~/stockintel` on `main`, with PM2 frontend + backend online.

## EC2 deploy (production)

- Host: `ubuntu@13.234.68.89`
- Key: `C:\Users\Jay\Downloads\Broker-key.pem`
- App dir: `~/stockintel`
- Prefer piping a bash script over SSH from PowerShell (`@'...'@ | ssh ... bash`); bash heredocs fail in PowerShell.

On the server:

1. `git fetch origin main && git reset --hard origin/main`
2. Backend: `source venv/bin/activate`, `pip install -r requirements.txt` if deps changed, `pm2 restart backend --update-env`
3. Frontend: stop apps if RAM is tight (~2GB box), `npm run build`, ensure standalone static copy (postbuild or `cp -r .next/static .next/standalone/.next/` and `public` → `.next/standalone/`), then `pm2 restart frontend --update-env`
4. `pm2 save` and verify `curl` health + https://getstockreport.com

Also see repo `deploy.sh` and `docs/private/GetStockReport-Specification.md` (confidential — do not publish).

## Env reminders on deploy

- Never commit `.env` / secrets.
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` is bake-time — set on the server **before** `npm run build`.
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` / `API_PUBLIC_URL` must be `https://getstockreport.com` with **no** trailing `/api`.

## Exceptions

- Skip auto-deploy only for pure docs/rules, local-only experiments, or when the user says not to deploy.
- If deploy fails (TS build, OOM, PM2), fix forward and redeploy until local/git/EC2 match again.
